        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "DyCl3·6H2O (0.053 g, 0.140 mmol) was added to a methanol solution (20 mL) of Na4daps (0.050 g, 0.105 mmol) and stirred at 35 °C for 30 min to a yellow solution. Separately, a solution of ZnCl2 (0.09 g, 0.070 mmol) was basified to pH 7.3 with 0.1 M methanolic (CH3)4N(OH). The basic zinc solution was added to the yellow solution and the mixture refluxed for 2 h. After cooling, slow evaporation gave yellow crystals of [Zn2Dy4(daps)2(Hdaps)(Cl)3(OH)2(CH3OH)(H2O)5]·0.5CH3OH·5H2O. Air-drying removed lattice methanol, isolating Zn2Dy4·5H2O. An analogue solvate was also obtained from Na4daps, DyCl3·6H2O and ZnCl2 in a 1:1:1 molar ratio in lower yield.",
